{
  "schema": 1,
  "name": "Prestige reopens Worldforged pickups only for the prestiging character (#5738)",
  "contract": [
    "CoA players explicitly describe collecting Worldforged items again after prestige: https://www.reddit.com/r/ProjectAscension/comments/1vyu132/coa_worldforged_recovery/ . The user authorized restoration if external evidence supported it.",
    "The reported Stormbringer class 16 and an ordinary Warrior control each open the real phase-1 Mossy Bag spawn 6941971 (90626, item 450672) and Bundle of Dried Corn 6941623 (515443, item 450993). Each pickup pays once per character before prestige, including after relog.",
    "Changing the Stormbringer's level to 1 without prestige must not reopen its spent bag. Normal Chromie prestige from level 60 / Lightning specialization 15 must preserve both existing items and reopen both pickups after relog. The bag is collected at level 1 and the corn after leveling to its item equip requirement of 3; that equip requirement does not gate looting.",
    "Collecting both again leaves them spent after another relog, while the control character's ledger stays spent. Rewards and ledger outcomes are produced by native opening, looting, prestige and relog; none are seeded.",
    " A second actual Chromie prestige is followed by an immediate Bag claim before relogging. After relogging that Bag must stay spent, while the Corn not yet claimed in the new cycle must still be reclaimable; both third items survive another relog.",
    "Mossy Bag has MaxCount 1. Prestige preserves the old bag; duplicate native loot remains rejected, then removing the old bag permits recovery from the reset pickup. Corn copies are retained across both cycles."
  ],
